  "chapter": 348,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 52 Chapter 348\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 2770-C, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to enacting the\n        Jonah Bichotte Cowan law relating to  pre-term  labor  care  and\n        directing  the  commissioner  of  health to require hospitals to\n        provide pre-term labor patients with information  regarding  the\n        potential health effects of pre-term labor and pre-term delivery\n        on an expectant mother and on her fetus\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill enacts the Jonah Bichotte Cowan Law. The bill creates stand-\nards  of  care  for  situations  where an expectant mother presents to a\nhospital with concerns about being in pre-term labor, and also  requires\nthat  hospitals  provide information on the risks of pre-term labor in a\nleaflet provided to new and expectant parents.\n \n  I am in full support of the goals of this legislation, and am grateful\nto Assemblymember Bichotte for elevating this issue and  proposing  this\nlaw named in memory of her son.\n \n  I  have secured changes to the bill with the Legislature to ensure its\nsuccessful implementation. The informational leaflet referenced  in  the\nbill  that  is  aimed to give notice to expectant parents on the risk of\npre-term labor, is most often given to parents after delivery  of  their\nchild,  upon  discharge  from  the hospital. I have secured an agreement\nwith the Legislature to include this important information  on  pre-term\nlabor  in a different pamphlet that will be given to all expectant moth-\ners during the course of their prenatal healthcare visits  and  at  pre-\nbooking in anticipation of labor.\n \n  The  changes  to  the  bill  also include requiring hospitals to adopt\nprotocols for assessing, treating, and  discharging  expectant  patients\nwho present to the hospital in accordance with current federal and state\nrequirements, and directing the Department of Health to provide emergen-\ncy  room  staff  informational  materials  on these requirements. On the\nbasis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2020
 },
